 is drawn as a dot."],"citations":["Typical work: works published 2023 have a median of 0 citations each.","Most cited works: the top 10% of works published in 2023 have at least 4 citations each, the highest P90 in the chart.","Not yet cited: more than half of the works published 2023–2025 have no citations so far. This is expected for recent works and is not a sign of low quality.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 1 of 1 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2023: mean 1.4, median 0, top work 9. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Recent years: works from 2024–2025 have had less than three years to be cited, so their values will rise.","Small base: the values for 2018–2022 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2017 and 2026 have fewer than 10 works (2017: 8, 2026: 4), too few for a band. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."]}}}